Z||000000||FieroGT||04-12-2000||11:35 AM||||Hi, everybody. It's been a while since I've posted. I can't believe that this website has grown so much since I registered. I think there was less than 300 members when I registered. <P>I'm sad to say that I've disposed of one of my Fieros, the '85 SE V6. It's moved to good hands though, since I've given it to my brother, who is a poor college student. He had a Conquest TSi, which took a dump on him a few months ago. At least the Fiero is still in the family. I still have my '86 GT with the nice leather seat conversion, and I still get the occasional e-mail asking questions on it. As always, I'm more than happy to respond (although it does take a couple days, sometimes). I can't believe how many websites have my original installation procedure posted! Even Mr. Mikes has it! I am truly flattered. <P>And I'm glad to see that the off-topic section that I had pestered Cliff for is doing well. Kudos to you, Cliff!<P>Other projects have been keeping me from my Fiero, lately. I actually put less than 4,000 miles a year on it, now. I just purchased a '92 Saturn SC to beat around in, and I laid my motorcycle down a couple of weeks ago, so those things have been keeping me busy. I just finished the bike, (Now there's some REALLY expensive plastic!!) and am working on straightening out a rich running condition I have with the Saturn. <P>Good to see that everyone is doing well, and look forward to meeting with some of you is you decide to attend the KitCar Nationals at Carlisle, PA this year. I'm going to the spring show in a couple weeks, as well. Let me know if any of you are going!<P>John<p>[This message has been edited by FieroGT (edited 04-12-2000).]||||reg||5
